messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf George likes music, he wants to compose. If George has access to a program, he can compose. If George can compose and wants to compose, he will compose.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If George will not compose, George can not compose.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine the truth value of the statement "If George will not compose, George cannot compose," we need to analyze the given information step by step.\n\n1.**Given Information:**\n   - If George likes music, he wants to compose.\n   - If George has access to a program, he can compose.\n   - If George can compose and wants to compose, he will compose.\n\n2.**Statement to Evaluate:**\n   - If George will not compose, George cannot compose.\n\n3.**Reasoning:**\n   - Let\'s denote the following:\n     - \\( L \\): George likes music.\n     - \\( W \\): George wants to compose.\n     - \\( C \\): George can compose.\n     - \\( P \\): George has access to a program.\n     - \\( F \\): George will compose.\n\n   - From the given information, we have:\n     - \\( L \\rightarrow W \\) (If George likes music, he wants to compose.)\n     - \\( P \\rightarrow C \\) (If George has access to a program, he can compose.)\n     - \\( (C \\land W) \\rightarrow F \\) (If George can compose and wants to compose, he will compose.)\n\n4.**Analyzing the Statement:**\n   - The statement "If George will not compose, George cannot compose" can be written as:\n     - \\( \\neg F \\rightarrow \\neg C \\) (If George will not compose, he cannot compose.)\n\n5.**Checking for Contradictions:**\n   - We need to check if the statement is consistent with the given information.\n   - Consider the scenario where George likes music (\\( L \\)) and has access to a program (\\( P \\)):\nIf George will not compose, then it\'s because he cannot compose.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
