nts, then they do not eat salads regularly.**\n6.**If people visit the gym at least once a day, then they always fulfill their daily nutritional intakes.**\n7.**It is either both true that Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and she has a good relationship with her parents, or it is true that Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents.**\n\nNow, let\'s examine the implications of these statements:\n\n- From point 2, if Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home, she would eat salads regularly.\n- From point 3, since Taylor eats salads regularly, she must have fulfilled her nutritional daily intakes.\n- From point 4, if Taylor has a good relationship with her parents, she would fulfill her nutritional daily intakes.\n- From point 5, if Taylor has a good relationship with her parents, she would not eat salads regularly.If Taylor does not visit the gym at least once a day, she would never fulfill her daily nutritional intakes.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
