do not develop strong bonds with their family members.**\n   - This suggests that if Luke does not live at home regularly, he may not develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\n5.**If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.**\n   - This implies that if Luke spends a lot of time with his siblings, he may not live at home regularly.\n\n6.**Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.**\nBased on the information provided, it can be inferred that Luke does not complain frequently about annoying siblings. The details suggest that he likely does not have siblings his age, does not spend much time with any siblings he may have, and probably lives at home regularly. The statement "Luke complains often about annoying siblings" is not consistent with the given information and is therefore doubtful.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
