messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nMonkeypox is an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus. Monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans. Humans are mammals. Mammals are animals. Symptons of Monkeypox include fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on. People feel tired when they get a glu.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? There is an animal.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine if the statement "There is an animal" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, we need to analyze the information provided step by step.\n\n1.**Identify the key elements in the context:**.\n   - Monkeypox is an infectious disease caused by the monkeypox virus.\n   - Monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans.\n   - Humans are mammals.\n   - Mammals are animals.\n   - Symptoms of Monkeypox include fever, headache, muscle pains, feeling tired, and so on.\n   - People feel tired when they get a flu.\n\n2.**Analyze the relationship between the monkeypox virus and animals:**.\n   - The context states that the monkeypox virus can occur in certain animals, including humans.\n   - This implies that there are indeed animals that can be infected with the monkeypox virus.\n\n3.**Consider the definition of an animal:**.\n   - The context defines mammals as animals.\n   - Since the monkeypox virus can occur in certain mammals (humans), it follows that there are animals involved in the transmission of the virus.\n\n4.**Evaluate the statement "There is an animal":**.\n   - Based on the information provided, there are indeed animals (specifically, humans) that can be infected with the monkeypox virus.\n   - Therefore, the statement "There is an animal" is true.There is no animal.. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 86%|########5 | 175/204 [00:47<00:04,  6.17it/s] 86%|########6 | 176/204 [00:47<00:04,  6.20it/s]
